        "summary": "Prior plan returned no_progress while both type-305 enemies stayed outside effective tear range (~195) at distances of ~323 and ~449 px. This revision keeps a single primary profile focused on closing the gap: finish_first targeting of the nearer enemy (3369478536:3), keep_range with a lower 0.35 minimum ratio and 0.75 maximum to commit into firing lanes between rock clusters, and shorter predictive lead (8 ticks) with movement inheritance for their slow drift. Evasion uses max_clearance with a small 4 px margin so dodging does not pull back out of range; escape keeps a modest 20-tick route check because doors can be shut by these enemies. The cautious profile is only for the concrete condition of health dropping below 60%, where threat_first targeting, wider kite band, minimal_shift evasion and cheaper fire gating reduce exposure near fireplaces and unknown type-305 behavior. Type-305 attack pattern remains unverified by the catalog, so no behavior-specific tactic is asserted.",
